{"name":"Pluto","hex":"#34acb1","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Pluto","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["The Greco-Roman god of the underworld.","The largest dwarf planet and formerly the ninth planet, represented by the symbol ♇ or ⯓, both now used mostly in astrology. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Pluto"}],"entries":[{"title":"Pluto","blocks":[{"text":"Pluto is a dwarf planet in the Kuiper belt, a ring of bodies beyond the orbit of Neptune. It is the ninth-largest and tenth-most-massive known object to directly orbit the Sun. It is the largest known trans-Neptunian object by volume by a small margin, but is less massive than Eris. Like other Kuiper belt objects, Pluto is made primarily of ice and rock and is much smaller than the inner planets. Pluto has roughly one-sixth the mass of the Moon and one-third of its volume. Originally considered a planet, its status was changed when astronomers adopted a new definition of the word with new criteria."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ca/Pluto_in_True_Color_-_High-Res.png/330px-Pluto_in_True_Color_-_High-Res.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pluto","wikidata":"Q339"},{"title":"Pluto (film series)","blocks":[{"text":"Pluto is a series of American animated comedy short films produced by Walt Disney Productions. The series started in 1937 with Pluto's Quin-puplets and ended in 1951 with Cold Turkey. The series stars the titular character Pluto, introduced in the Mickey Mouse film series as Mickey's pet dog, in addition to having recurring appearances by previously known characters such as Minnie Mouse, Figaro the Kitten, and Mickey Mouse, and also introduced well-known characters such as the chipmunk duo Chip 'n' Dale."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/e/ed/AWaltDisneyPluto_opening_title.jpg/330px-AWaltDisneyPluto_opening_title.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pluto_(film_series)","wikidata":"Q3906821"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f4/Pluto_discovery_plates.gif/500px-Pluto_discovery_plates.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f4/Pluto_discovery_plates.gif/1280px-Pluto_discovery_plates.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f4/Pluto_discovery_plates.gif/500px-Pluto_discovery_plates.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APluto_discovery_plates.gif"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/01/Clyde_W._Tombaugh.jpeg/250px-Clyde_W._Tombaugh.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/01/Clyde_W._Tombaugh.jpeg/500px-Clyde_W._Tombaugh.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/01/Clyde_W._Tombaugh.jpeg/250px-Clyde_W._Tombaugh.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AClyde_W._Tombaugh.jpeg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/af/Animation_of_Pluto_orbit.gif/500px-Animation_of_Pluto_orbit.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/af/Animation_of_Pluto_orbit.gif/500px-Animation_of_Pluto_orbit.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"An animation of Pluto's orbit from 1850 to 2097.mw-parser-outp